#: ../../ai.rst:208
msgid "Model Context Protocol (MCP)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:210
msgid "Remix supports **Model Context Protocol (MCP)** servers, which give the RemixAI access to external tools and libraries during agentic workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:212
msgid "You can manage the MCP servers available to you in **Settings > RemixAI Assistant**. Here you can turn the available servers on and off, depending on your preferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:214
msgid "Remix MCP Connected Services panel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:218
msgid "The following MCP servers are available in RemixAI:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:220
msgid "**Remix IDE Server** (Built-in) – Always connected. Gives the AI direct access to your workspace files and IDE features such as compilation, file management, and Slither static analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:223
msgid "**OpenZeppelin Contracts** – Gives the AI access to OpenZeppelin's audited contract library, so it can suggest secure, battle-tested implementations rather than generating patterns from scratch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:226
msgid "**Web Search** – Allows the AI to retrieve up-to-date information such as recent protocol changes, audit reports, and external documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:229
msgid "The following MCP servers are additionally available to **Beta testers**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:231
msgid "**ethSkills** – A curated Ethereum knowledge base designed specifically for AI agents. It covers production-ready guidance across gas costs, L2s, token standards, DeFi protocols, security patterns, contract auditing, and more, helping the AI avoid stale or hallucinated answers about Ethereum development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:235
msgid "**Alchemy** – Allows the AI to query live on-chain data including account balances, transaction histories, and contract state via Alchemy's infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:237
msgid "**Etherscan** – Allows the AI to look up deployed contracts, inspect verified source code, and retrieve transaction data directly from the block explorer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:239
msgid "**The Graph API** – Allows the AI to query indexed blockchain data via GraphQL subgraphs, useful for retrieving protocol analytics and historical event data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:244
msgid "Sample prompts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:246
msgid "The examples below show how to phrase requests to get the most out of the RemixAI Assistant. Each section explains the intent behind the prompt type and gives one example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:248
msgid "**Writing contracts**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:250
msgid "Ask RemixAI to generate a contract from a plain-language description. Be specific about the behaviour you want (access control, token standards, limits) and the AI will produce a starting implementation you can refine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:252
msgid "*Write an ERC-20 token contract with a mint function restricted to the owner and a maximum supply of 1 million tokens.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:254
msgid "**Security review**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:256
msgid "Ask RemixAI to analyse a specific contract or the active file for vulnerabilities. You can target a particular class of issue or ask for a general review. Slither static analysis is built into the Remix IDE Server, so the AI can run it and incorporate the results without any additional setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:258
msgid "*Review the active contract for reentrancy vulnerabilities and suggest fixes.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:260
msgid "**Using OpenZeppelin** *(OpenZeppelin MCP)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:262
msgid "Ask RemixAI to suggest or apply an OpenZeppelin implementation instead of writing custom logic. The AI has access to the full OpenZeppelin library and can recommend the right base contract for your use case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:264
msgid "*Replace the access control in this contract with OpenZeppelin's Ownable.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:266
msgid "**Querying live on-chain data** *(Alchemy / Etherscan, Beta)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:268
msgid "Ask RemixAI to look up real-time blockchain data such as balances, transactions, or verified source code. Useful for investigating a deployed contract or checking an address without leaving the IDE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:270
msgid "*Fetch the verified source code and recent transactions for this contract address: 0x...*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:272
msgid "**Querying indexed protocol data** *(The Graph, Beta)*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:274
msgid "Ask RemixAI to query a subgraph for aggregated or historical data. Useful for retrieving protocol-level metrics or event histories that are not available from a single contract call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:276
msgid "*Get the total value locked in Aave on Ethereum over the last 7 days using a subgraph query.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:278
msgid "**General Solidity and Ethereum questions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:280
msgid "Ask RemixAI about language features, best practices, or protocol mechanics. The Web Search MCP server allows it to retrieve up-to-date information, so it can answer questions about recent changes that postdate its training data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:282
msgid "*What changed in Solidity 0.8.24 that could affect a contract I wrote for 0.8.20?*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:285
msgid "Code completion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ai.rst:287
msgid "When you type a space or start a new line, the RemixAI Assistant may propose code suggestions. This feature is known as **code completion**."
